23022	{"artifactId":"DEF-c66d49bb81925886","entry":{"id":"review-71aab016dfc8b4931e983000549fab87","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-26T05:11:13.236Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"define","stage":"define","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"p01","ref":"4/c5","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The approved common-artifact S004 LLD provides a reusable uniform artifact store and durable-history substrate.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:13 attributes to S004 a per-repository ArtifactStore, History and LifecycleService, durable framed log/feedback sidecars, and a file-backed WriteJournal with priorHeadHash recovery protection. These support the claimed reusable artifact-store and durable-history substrate. S004/LLD.md:1 confirms artifact identity LLD-2f27754d4ad00b8e-s4.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p02","ref":"4/c6","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Artifact content hashing uses description, body and citations as its content boundary.","evidence":"src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:102 declares contentHash(description: string, payload: { readonly body: unknown; readonly citations: unknown }), confirming the three inputs. However, line 104 contains only the closing brace; the hashing implementation is absent from the supplied evidence. The truncated grep results do not establish which inputs are actually hashed or whether they define the complete content boundary.","action":"Gather the contentHash implementation, including line 103, to verify the fields included in the hash.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The signature supports the input inventory but does not verify the hashing boundary.","options":["Provide the function body and reassess the content-boundary claim.","Narrow the premise to the verified signature: contentHash accepts description and a payload containing body and citations."]}},{"claimId":"p03","ref":"4/c6","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Usage metadata can remain outside the artifact content-hash boundary if relevant artifact writers preserve that metadata.","evidence":"src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts:102 declares contentHash(description, payload: { body; citations }), consistent with metadata being outside its explicit inputs. However, no function body or relevant artifact-writer reads were supplied. The truncated grep provides no meta.tokenUsage matches or evidence that writers preserve usage metadata, so the premise is unverifiable.","action":"Provide the contentHash implementation and relevant artifact-writer reads showing whether meta.tokenUsage survives artifact updates.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The supplied signature supports the proposed boundary but does not establish hashing behavior or metadata preservation.","options":["Gather the hash implementation and writer evidence before retaining the premise as verified.","Reword the premise as a design requirement: exclude usage metadata from content hashing and require relevant writers to preserve it."]}},{"claimId":"p04","ref":"4/c7","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The shared provider response type declares token counters as optional.","evidence":"The reads show only `export interface LLMResponse {` at src/shared/types.ts:61 and its closing brace at :87. Neither exposes the token-counter declarations. The truncated grep includes a partial quotation at plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:17, but it stops before the usage field and counters. Their optionality is therefore unverifiable from the supplied evidence.","action":"Gather src/shared/types.ts:62–86 to verify whether the usage object and its individual token counters are optional.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The supplied evidence omits the declarations needed to assess the premise.","options":["Read the full LLMResponse body and retain the premise if the counter declarations confirm it.","Revise the premise to distinguish optional usage from optional individual counters if the full declaration requires that distinction."]}},{"claimId":"p05","ref":"3/c1","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"MED","premise":"The PRD ownership section assigns canonical usage history to an append-only collection under each owning artifact's meta.tokenUsage and treats pending storage as recovery storage.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:5 identifies the reviewed LLD’s meta.tokenUsage.events as authoritative and assigns other activities to their owning artifact JSON. It describes unresolved targets as a visible unassigned/pending bucket until explicitly reconciled. It does not establish append-only collections under every artifact’s meta.tokenUsage or characterize pending storage as recovery storage. docs/model-token-usage-prd.html:1 contains only the document header and provides no additional support.","action":"Verify the append-only, universal meta.tokenUsage placement, and recovery-storage claims against the relevant PRD content, or narrow the premise to the ownership and pending-reconciliation rules supplied.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The evidence supports ownership attribution but does not verify the claimed storage contract; it supplies no contradiction establishing a concrete implementation failure.","options":["Narrow the premise to authoritative owning-artifact records, LLD meta.tokenUsage.events, and a pending bucket for unresolved targets.","Supply PRD passages explicitly establishing append-only meta.tokenUsage collections and pending storage’s recovery role, then reassess."]}},{"claimId":"p06","ref":"k2","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"MED","premise":"The PRD ownership evidence supports stable attempt identities, one charged owner per attempt, idempotent transport replay and separate accounting for distinct model retries.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:5 states that an attempt has exactly one callId, one charged artifact and one owning work item, and that distinct physical attempts each count. This supports attempt identity, single ownership and separate retry accounting. It does not explicitly establish identity preservation or deduplication on transport replay. docs/model-token-usage-prd.html:1 contains only the HTML header and adds no supporting detail.","action":"Provide evidence for idempotent transport replay, or narrow the premise to the ownership and distinct-attempt accounting rules established by the supplied evidence.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The replay guarantee is not established by the supplied evidence; no concrete build-breaking contradiction is shown.","options":["Supply a passage explicitly requiring transport replays to preserve attempt identity and avoid duplicate charges.","Narrow the premise to one callId and charged owner per attempt, with separate accounting for distinct physical attempts."]}},{"claimId":"p07","ref":"k7","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The PRD ownership evidence assigns reviews to the reviewed LLD, task work to TASK and shared story validation or code review to BUILD.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:5 explicitly assigns LLD authoring, correction and design reviews to the reviewed LLD’s meta.tokenUsage.events; task implementation, probes, repair and task validation to TASK JSON; and story-wide validation and post-build code review to story BUILD JSON, with CR references. This confirms the stated ownership assignments.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p08","ref":"4/c2","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The PRD counting section allows disclosed aggregate or unknown observation granularity without claiming fabricated physical-call facts.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:7 reproduces the counting section: invocation-level per-model totals retain their granularity with “physical call count unavailable”; aggregate-only integration does not satisfy complete per-call coverage. It also requires unknown values to remain disclosed, separates estimates, and prohibits adding overlapping aggregate and leaf observations. These provisions confirm the premise.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p09","ref":"k4","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The PRD counting evidence requires distinguishable measurement states, disjoint cache buckets, no double counting of reasoning and no summation of cumulative snapshots.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:7 explicitly separates reported, estimated, unknown, instrumented zero and legacy absence; defines uncached input, cache reads and cache writes as separate buckets; identifies reasoning as an output subset that must never be added again; and requires durable-baseline deltas for session-cumulative counters, stating “Never sum successive cumulative snapshots.” This confirms all four requirements in the premise.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p10","ref":"k3","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The PRD integrity evidence requires preservation of original observations and visible conflicts for invalid correction, reconciliation or attribution histories.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:9 explicitly requires corrections to “Preserve the original,” concurrent edits or forked corrections to “remain visible conflicts until reconciled,” and cycles, forks, mismatched owners or nonexistent targets to produce partial/conflict notices. It also requires validating owner/call identity when merging immutable events. These requirements support the premise.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p11","ref":"k5","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The PRD integrity evidence requires usage-only updates to preserve approved content state and requires supported artifact operations to preserve acknowledged usage.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:9 explicitly requires usage-only appends not to change description/body/citations hashes, invalidate approval, or reset content revision. It also requires every artifact writer, codec, import/export, workflow regeneration and merge to preserve the usage collection, and identical duplicate events to be acknowledged without another charge. These requirements confirm both parts of the premise.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p12","ref":"k6","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The PRD integrity evidence requires durable acknowledged appends and recoverable attachment before artifact creation without fabricating content or rerunning inference.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:9 requires serialized durable appends, acknowledgment of identical duplicates, a durable started event before dispatch, and recovery of staged appends and pending-attachment rows after restart. It also prohibits model re-execution for telemetry and guessed backfills, supporting the premise's durability, recoverable attachment, and no-fabrication requirements.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p13","ref":"k9","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"MED","premise":"The PRD integrity evidence requires explicit legacy, unsupported and malformed accounting outcomes and forbids silent loss or truncation of retained history.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:9 explicitly requires tolerance of older artifacts, unsupported versions displaying “Usage unavailable” rather than zero, preservation of retained accounting, and visible correction conflicts. It does not explicitly specify a general malformed-data outcome or prohibit truncation by name. docs/model-token-usage-prd.html:1 supplies only the HTML header and does not establish those additional claims.","action":"Narrow the premise to the supported requirements, or supply evidence explicitly establishing malformed-data outcomes and retained-history truncation rules.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The evidence supports most of the premise but does not fully establish its stated explicit requirements.","options":["Reword the premise to require older-artifact tolerance, explicit unsupported-version and correction-conflict outcomes, and preservation of retained accounting without silent loss.","Retain the premise and provide additional PRD evidence explicitly requiring malformed-data outcomes and prohibiting retained-history truncation."]}},{"claimId":"p14","ref":"3/k10","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The implementation plan defines TU1 completion independently of later capture, controller, hierarchy and board epics.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:11 reproduces the implementation plan: TU1 has no required predecessors, owns storage and accounting semantics, and explicitly excludes provider instrumentation, workflow dispatch, subtree totals and board UI. Its exit criteria cover preservation, durable append/recovery, reconciliation and published contracts. The planning boundary states that an epic's completion must not depend on an unfinished successor, and the build sequence gates TU1 before TU2–TU5.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p15","ref":"3","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"MED","premise":"The related epic allocation assigns automatic capture and provider normalization to TU2, controller reporting to TU3, hierarchy read models to TU4 and client presentation to TU5.","evidence":"plans/model-token-usage-implementation.md:1 confirms only the plan title. docs/model-token-usage-prd.html:1 shows the PRD HTML header and title. Neither supplied read establishes the TU2–TU5 allocations, so the premise is unverifiable.","action":"Gather the epic allocation passages defining TU2–TU5 and verify each responsibility against them.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The supplied evidence contains no allocation details from which to derive a safe correction.","options":["Provide the epic passages assigning responsibilities to TU2–TU5.","Remove the allocation claim until supporting passages are available."]}},{"claimId":"p16","ref":"k8","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"AGENTS.md requires daemon-owned database access, CLI-mediated cloud inference, sequential provider calls and preservation of critical model capability.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:19 reproduces AGENTS.md requirements for all four claims: architectural rule 1 assigns all DB access to the daemon; project principles and rule 2 require cloud inference through claude/codex CLI subprocesses; LLM provider conventions require sequential awaits rather than Promise.all; and model-tiering principles require critical roles to remain at or above the high tier through coreFloor.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p17","ref":"c9","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The evidence entry at line 21 excerpts the common artifact store implementation.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:21 explicitly labels c9 as `Source src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts` and excerpts `export class ArtifactStore`, including its constructor, history accessor, read, readWithHistory, write, update, and updateAndLog methods. This confirms the cited evidence entry excerpts the artifact store implementation.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p18","ref":"c10","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The evidence entry at line 23 excerpts the common artifact journal implementation.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:23 contains the c10 entry labeled `Source src/workflow/artifact-core/journal.ts` and excerpts headHashOf, StagedOperation, WriteJournal, createMemoryJournal, and createFileJournal. The read of src/workflow/artifact-core/journal.ts:1 also confirms the source path exists. This confirms the premise that line 23 excerpts the common artifact journal implementation.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p19","ref":"c12","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The evidence entry at line 25 excerpts the TU1 scope step output.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:25 contains entry c12, labels its source as plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-scope.json, and excerpts JSON with decision, scope, notify, flavorEvidence, evidence, and analyzeBundles fields. The source file is present; its line 1 is an opening JSON brace. This confirms the cited entry excerpts the TU1 scope output.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p20","ref":"c13","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The evidence entry at line 27 excerpts the TU1 frame step output.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:27 contains the c13 entry, identifies plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-frame.json as its source, and excerpts the frame JSON, including summary, problem, constraints, requirements and citations. The source file also exists, with line 1 containing its opening brace.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p21","ref":"c14","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The evidence entry at line 29 excerpts the TU1 stories step output.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:29 contains c14, names plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-stories.json as its source, and excerpts a JSON stories payload containing stories s1–s4 and citations. The source file also resolves at line 1. This confirms the stated evidence entry.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p22","ref":"c11","kind":"citation","severity":"LOW","premise":"The evidence entry at line 31 excerpts the TU1 grounding analyze bundle.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:31 contains the c11 entry naming plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-grounding.json as its source and excerpting a JSON grounding bundle with capturedAt, focus, bundle, explorationOutputs, and limitations. This confirms the stated citation premise.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p23","ref":"6.1–6.4/Extends","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"MED","premise":"The grounding bundle cited as c11 supports the existing artifact foundation extended by all four proposed stories.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:31 identifies c11 as the grounding bundle and records ArtifactStore, decodeArtifactHead, createRepoLifecycle, prepareArtifactWrite, and common-artifact S002/S004 design references. This supports an existing storage and lifecycle foundation. However, the supplied evidence contains no contents or Extends relationships for STORY-c66d49bb81925886-s1 through s4, so support for all four stories cannot be verified. The bundle itself requires direct source reads during design and disclaims exhaustive coverage.","action":"Supply each story's Extends text and map its foundation claims to c11 evidence, or narrow the premise to the shared foundation that c11 establishes.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The shared foundation is supported, but the four-story applicability claim lacks story-level evidence.","options":["Provide the four stories' Extends sections and evidence mapping for each.","Narrow the premise to say c11 identifies the existing artifact storage and lifecycle foundation, leaving story-specific applicability for separate verification."]}},{"claimId":"p24","ref":"s2/Depends on","kind":"ordering","severity":"MED","premise":"Story s2 requires the usage identity and reconciliation semantics defined by s1 before implementing durable submission and recovery.","evidence":"The only supplied read, plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-stories.json:1, contains `{`. It provides no story contents or dependency semantics, so the claimed s2 dependency on s1 is unverifiable.","action":"Provide the s1 usage identity and reconciliation definitions and s2 dependency and recovery requirements to verify the ordering.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The evidence does not support confirming or correcting the dependency.","options":["Gather the relevant s1 and s2 artifact passages and reassess the dependency.","Mark the ordering premise as unverified pending evidence."]}},{"claimId":"p25","ref":"s3/Depends on","kind":"ordering","severity":"MED","premise":"Story s3 requires the durable usage persistence implemented by s2 before establishing preservation across artifact operations.","evidence":"The only supplied evidence is plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-stories.json:1 containing `{`. It provides no story content or dependency information to verify that s3 requires s2's durable usage persistence.","action":"Gather the s2 persistence requirements and s3 preservation requirements and dependency declarations to verify the ordering.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The supplied evidence does not establish or contradict the dependency; no evidence-derived text correction is safe.","options":["Provide the relevant s2 and s3 artifact excerpts to verify the dependency.","Provide the relevant story records from plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-stories.json."]}},{"claimId":"p26","ref":"s4/Depends on","kind":"ordering","severity":"MED","premise":"Story s4 requires both s2 persistence and s3 lifecycle preservation before providing daemon accounting access and operational guarantees.","evidence":"The only supplied evidence is plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-stories.json:1 containing `{`. It provides no story definitions or dependency relationships and cannot verify that s4 requires both s2 and s3.","action":"Provide the s2, s3, and s4 story definitions and s4 dependency fields, then verify the claimed ordering.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The supplied evidence does not support a safe correction to the dependency premise.","options":["Gather the story definitions and dependency fields to verify the ordering.","Mark the dependency premise unverified pending supporting evidence."]}}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":11,"low":15},"reviewedAt":"2026-10-26T05:11:13.236Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6.1-sol","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
