rt, serialized per-artifact appends, and concurrent immutable-event merging without discarding conflicts. Its artifact contract requires binding pending usage to the intended stable artifact ID and merging idempotently when the first valid artifact is persisted, without fabricating an approved design body. Failed recording must retry the append rather than the model call; crash recovery must not re-execute inference to collect telemetry. TU04 and TU07 explicitly require recovery and concurrent appends to preserve history and lose neither event. These confirm the premise as a requirement, not an existing implementation claim.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p18","ref":"5/k7","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"Source c1 assigns review charges to the reviewed LLD, task work to TASK and shared story validation/code review to BUILD, preserving dispatch ownership and explicit transfer provenance.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review2-evidence.txt:1 explicitly assigns LLD authoring/correction/design reviews to the reviewed LLD’s meta.tokenUsage.events, task implementation/probes/repair/validation to TASK JSON, and story-wide validation/post-build code review to BUILD JSON. It also requires preserving the owner recorded at dispatch and recording explicit attribution transfer/effective mapping on reparenting while preserving historical provenance and counting each call once. These are source requirements, not claims of existing implementation.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p19","ref":"5/k8","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing architectural conventions place persistence behind daemon interfaces and require clients to avoid direct database access.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:19 (c8, source AGENTS.md) explicitly states that the daemon owns all DB access, CLI/MCP/workbench communicate via IPC only, and client