verity":"LOW","premise":"Existing artifact content hashing covers description, body and citations.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c6.txt:1 shows src/workflow/artifact-core/lifecycle.ts contentHash hashing canonicalJson({ description, body: payload.body, citations: payload.citations }) with SHA-256, confirming all three fields are covered.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p03","ref":"4/c7","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The shared provider response permits usage to be absent, requires inputTokens and outputTokens when usage exists, and permits cache counters to be absent.","evidence":"The read at plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c7.txt:1 shows LLMResponse with `usage?: { inputTokens: number; outputTokens: number; cacheReadTokens?: number | undefined; cacheCreationTokens?: number | undefined; } | undefined`. This confirms optional usage, required input/output counters within usage, and optional cache counters.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p04","ref":"4/c7","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Optional provider-response usage does not itself establish durable artifact-level accounting coverage.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c7.txt:1 shows LLMResponse.usage is optional API-response token metadata, containing token counts and optional cache counts. That interface establishes neither artifact attribution nor durable persistence, confirming the premise's limited claim. The truncated grep does not establish broader accounting coverage.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p05","ref":"4/c2","kind":"external-contract","severity":"LOW","premise":"The cited PRD permits disclosed aggregate or unknown source evidence and does not justify inventing per-call measurements when a source's physical-call granularity is unqualified.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c2.txt:1 explicitly requires retaining per-model invocation totals at that granularity with physical call count unavailable, permits aggregate fallback evidence, and keeps reported, estimated, and unknown values separate. It also states that aggregate-only integrations do not satisfy complete per-call coverage. This supports disclosing aggregate or unknown evidence without inventing per-call measurements.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p06","ref":"3/common-artifact-store","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"An existing generic common artifact core supplies the persistence substrate, lifecycle, journal and identity scheme that TU1 is intended to extend.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/grounding.json:1 locates ArtifactStore at src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts:102–417, createRepoLifecycle at repo-lifecycle.ts:27–35, and confirms store.ts and journal.ts exist. Its S002 documentation excerpt describes the shared reader/writer and identity from the s1 id module; its bundle explicitly identifies the common core as TU1's reuse substrate. plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:13 describes the durable journal, history and per-repository LifecycleService. These support the premise without requiring exhaustive caller coverage.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p07","ref":"3/TU2","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The roadmap assigns automatic provider capture and native Claude, Codex and Ollama usage normalization to TU2 rather than TU1.","evidence":"The supplied read of plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/roadmap.txt:1 explicitly states in TU1's scope boundary that it 'does not instrument model providers' and that 'provider adapters belong to TU2.' TU2 delivers automatic capture for daemon-dispatched requests, and its scope step 2 assigns normalization of supported Ollama, Claude CLI and Codex CLI paths. TU2's scope boundary also assigns it daemon instrumentation and provider-specific extraction.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p08","ref":"3/TU3","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The roadmap assigns controller-host capability negotiation, reporting and integrations to TU3 rather than TU1.","evidence":"The supplied read of plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/roadmap.txt:1 confirms TU3 owns the host capability/reporting handshake, IPC/MCP reporting surface, and supported controller integrations. Its contract ownership table assigns “Controller capability declarations and report ingestion” to TU3. TU1 establishes measurement boundaries and accounting semantics, while TU3 implements external reporting and host integrations.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p09","ref":"3/TU4-TU5","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The roadmap assigns work-hierarchy read models to TU4 and client presentation to TU5, excluding subtree totals and DeliverySnapshot or board usage presentation from TU1.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/roadmap.txt:1 explicitly excludes calculating work-item subtree totals and implementing board UI from TU1. Its TU4 scope assigns deterministic ownership rollups, delivery read-contract usage summaries, paged evidence and coherent snapshots to TU4; its TU5 scope assigns client contract consumption, board summaries and Usage drill-downs to TU5. The contract ownership table likewise assigns usage snapshots to TU4 and Delivery board presentation to TU5. This confirms the stated boundary, although the roadmap describes the delivery read contract without naming DeliverySnapshot explicitly.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p10","ref":"3/PRD","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"MED","premise":"The referenced PRD limits this initiative to token accounting and provenance rather than monetary pricing, invoice reconciliation, budgets, inference interception, model downgrades or raw prompt/response retention.","evidence":"roadmap.txt:1 explicitly excludes pricing, billing, budgets and automatic model selection, and prohibits storing prompts, completions or credentials. c3.txt:1 requires bounded normalized facts rather than raw transcripts and preserves existing provider access; c1.txt:1 establishes attribution/provenance and c2.txt:1 defines token accounting. These support most of the premise, but the supplied PRD excerpts do not explicitly exclude invoice reconciliation, inference interception or model downgrades. No concrete build-breaking contradiction is established.","action":"Narrow the premise to the evidenced boundaries, or supply the PRD passage establishing the remaining exclusions.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The evidence supports the core scope but does not verify every exclusion attributed specifically to the PRD.","options":["Reword the premise to cite the roadmap’s explicit exclusions of pricing, billing, budgets and automatic model selection, plus the PRD’s prohibition on raw transcript retention.","Retain the premise and supply the PRD scope passage explicitly addressing invoice reconciliation, inference interception and model downgrades."]}},{"claimId":"p11","ref":"k1","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"MED","premise":"The root-storage stakeholder decision requires one authoritative append-only events.avro file under <project>/.insrc/usage/<root-artifact-id>/ for each canonical epic, standalone or issue root, shared by its descendants.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-root-storage-decision.json:1 requires one data file per root artifact, appending root and child records under <project>/.insrc/usage/<artifact-id>/. However, it describes Avro as a proposed format pending physical schema/library qualification; it does not mandate events.avro or specify canonical epic, standalone, and issue root classification. No concrete build-breaking failure is established.","action":"Separate the confirmed root-storage requirement from the proposed format, filename, and root classification; qualify or independently ground those details.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The storage requirement is supported, but the premise presents proposed or ungrounded details as stakeholder mandates.","options":["Reword the premise to require one data file per root artifact containing appended root and child records, with Avro pending qualification.","Retain the detailed design as a proposal and supply separate evidence approving the format, filename, and canonical root classification."]}},{"claimId":"p12","ref":"k1","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"MED","premise":"The root-storage decision requires every ledger event to carry rootArtifactId and charged artifactId, excludes usage arrays from artifact JSON, and treats journals and Parquet caches as recovery or derived data.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-root-storage-decision.json:1 requires one data file per root artifact containing root and child records and explicitly says “Keep usage out of artifact JSON.” It describes a Parquet reporting cache, but does not require rootArtifactId or charged artifactId on every event, mention journals, or define recovery semantics. Those parts of the premise are unverifiable from the supplied evidence.","action":"Narrow the premise to the documented storage and reporting requirements, or supply evidence establishing the event fields and journal recovery semantics.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The evidence supports only part of the premise; retaining its additional requirements needs further grounding.","options":["Reword the premise to require one file per root artifact containing root and child records, exclude usage from artifact JSON, and describe the Parquet reporting cache.","Provide an authoritative schema or decision establishing mandatory event identifiers and journal/cache recovery semantics."]}},{"claimId":"p13","ref":"k2","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The c1 evidence supports one stable identity and one charged owner per actual attempt, idempotent transport replay, distinct retry consumption, and no extra charges for logical requests, native invocations, references or causal links.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c1.txt:1 states that each model attempt has exactly one callId, charged artifact and owning work item; multiple attempts of a logical request are distinct physical calls and count. It says invocationId is not a second charge, parentCallId is not a summation edge, and references are not additional usage edges. It also requires recovery using stable IDs and specifies that duplicate events and overlapping invocation/call observations are not additional usage, supporting idempotent replay.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p14","ref":"k3","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The c3 evidence supports retaining original observations while resolving corrections, overlap and ownership transfers, with invalid references, identity conflicts, forks and cycles exposed as conflicts.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c3.txt:1 explicitly says to keep all original observations and append corrections and attribution transfers as new facts. It requires the shared effective-event reducer before aggregation and says overlapping invocation/call observations are not additional usage. Corrections preserve originals and use the last unambiguous valid chain; cycles, forks, mismatched owners and nonexistent targets produce partial/conflict notices. Reused event IDs with different payloads are conflicts, and branch imports validate root/owner/call identity while retaining conflicting branches.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p15","ref":"k4","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"MED","premise":"The c2 evidence supports distinguishable reported, estimated, pending, unavailable and historical not-recorded states, disjoint cache buckets, no double counting of reasoning or cumulative snapshots, and no physical-call completeness claim from aggregate-only evidence.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c2.txt:1 supports separate reported/estimated/unknown values, legacy “Not recorded,” disjoint cache buckets, reasoning as an output subset, differenced cumulative counters, and no complete per-call coverage claim from aggregate-only evidence. It does not establish a distinct pending state or distinguish pending from unavailable.","action":"Narrow the premise to the states c2 establishes, or supply evidence defining pending and its distinction from unavailable.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"Most accounting claims are supported, but the asserted state inventory exceeds the supplied evidence. No concrete build-breaking consequence is established.","options":["Reword the state claim as reported, estimated, unknown and historical not-recorded, retaining the supported accounting claims.","Provide additional evidence defining pending and unavailable as distinct states."]}},{"claimId":"p16","ref":"k5","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"MED","premise":"The root-storage decision requires usage freshness to remain independent of artifact bytes and content approval state, ordinary content writes to preserve ledger bytes, and lifecycle operations and binary-safe reconciliation to preserve acknowledged history.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-root-storage-decision.json:1 requires one data file per root artifact, appending root and child records under <project>/.insrc/usage/<artifact-id>/, and keeping usage out of artifact JSON. It does not establish freshness independence from content approval, byte preservation during ordinary content writes, or acknowledged-history preservation during lifecycle operations and binary-safe reconciliation. Those requirements are unverifiable from the supplied evidence.","action":"Narrow the premise to the recorded storage decision, or supply evidence explicitly establishing the additional preservation and freshness requirements.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The cited decision supports separate root-scoped usage storage but does not substantiate the premise's additional behavioral guarantees.","options":["Narrow the premise to separate root-scoped usage files containing appended root and child records, with usage excluded from artifact JSON.","Retain the broader premise and provide explicit evidence for freshness, content-write, lifecycle, and binary-safe reconciliation guarantees."]}},{"claimId":"p17","ref":"k6","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"MED","premise":"The root-storage decision requires a daemon-owned single writer per repository/root, durable complete-block and directory-metadata acknowledgment, recovery preserving acknowledged events, and stable identity reservation before content exists.","evidence":"plans/evidence/model-token-usage-root-storage-decision.json:1 specifies one data file per root artifact, appending root and child records under <project>/.insrc/usage/<artifact-id>/, and daemon-owned DuckDB reporting. It does not establish a single writer, durable complete-block or directory-metadata acknowledgment, preservation of acknowledged events during recovery, or identity reservation before content exists. Those requirements are unverifiable from the supplied evidence.","action":"Supply evidence establishing the claimed durability, writer ownership, recovery, and identity requirements, or revise the premise to distinguish proposed requirements from the recorded root-storage decision.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The cited decision supports the storage layout but does not establish the additional guarantees; choosing whether to retain them requires confirmation.","options":["Retain the requirements and cite an explicit decision establishing each guarantee.","Reword the premise to describe only the per-root append storage layout established by the evidence.","Identify the additional guarantees as proposed requirements awaiting an architecture decision."]}},{"claimId":"p18","ref":"k7","kind":"cross-artifact","severity":"LOW","premise":"The c1 evidence assigns design review usage to the reviewed LLD, task work to TASK, and shared story validation or code review to BUILD, preserving dispatch ownership and explicit transfers without extra reference charges.","evidence":"plans/evidence/tu1-root-ledger-review/c1.txt:1 explicitly charges design reviews to the reviewed LLD, task implementation/probes/repair/validation to TASK, and story-wide validation/post-build code review to story BUILD. It states that references are not additional usage edges, preserves the owner recorded at dispatch, and requires explicit attribution transfers/effective mappings on reparenting while counting each call once.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"p19","ref":"k8","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Existing artifact contracts provide canonical identities and parent links, and persistence access is owned by the daemon.","evidence":"The supplied grep is truncated and shows artifactId/parentId primarily in design documents, including docs/epics/e1-delivery-read-model-daemon-from-E202610072ff0dfda/HLD.md:57 and :116; it does not establish the implemented canonical identity or parent-link contracts. plans/evidence/model-token-usage-root-storage-decision.json:1 specifies usage storage and daemon-owned DuckDB reporting, not those contracts. plans/evidence/model-token-usage-tu1-review-evidence.md:13 describes daemon-owned lifecycle persistence as a design's state after, while its state before explicitly says the daemon holds no ArtifactStore, History or LifecycleService. No supplied implementation reads resolve whether that design is implemented.","action":"Supply implementation evidence for canonical